E AX3063 648-region-argument.ax:15:23-27 region-argument "`pair` names one region `@r` for two of these arguments, and they do not live in the same region: parameter `x`, which lives in region `@s` against parameter `y`, which lives in region `@t`" ?"a region parameter is instantiated ONCE per call, like a type variable; every argument annotated with it must live in that one region. Pass values from one region, or give the parameters different region names"
